WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.022
In the 1930s, the Soviet Union did everything possible

00:00:04.022 --> 00:00:07.577
to demonstrate to the world how progressive communist ideas were.

00:00:07.577 --> 00:00:14.026
Outside the USSR, articles in the press appeared glorifying Stalin 
and his course for collectivisation,

00:00:14.026 --> 00:00:19.630
which in reality was forceful integration 
of individual households into collective farms.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:23.051
The articles were written by people like, for example,

00:00:23.051 --> 00:00:26.000
the celebrated American journalist Walter Duranty.

00:00:27.175 --> 00:00:30.690
However, Ukrainian villagers did not fit into the ideal picture. 

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:35.999
They did not want to join collective farms 
and voluntarily give away what they had earned.

00:00:35.999 --> 00:00:41.313
Resistance was also growing in Ukrainian cities, 
among the intelligentsia in particular.

00:00:41.313 --> 00:00:45.733
So the Soviet regime decided to break their resistance physically.

00:00:45.733 --> 00:00:51.077
In 1932–1933, millions of Ukrainians died.

00:00:51.077 --> 00:00:55.334
Rumours of this spread throughout the Soviet Union and abroad.

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:59.125
Even fabricated statistics could not stop them. 

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:06.141
Therefore, the Soviet government enabled its propaganda machine 
and hid the Holodomor for many decades

00:01:06.141 --> 00:01:10.015
behind silence and fake facts that should have been dispelled forever.

00:01:10.015 --> 00:01:15.923
However, even after the collapse of the Soviet Union, 
Russia, as its successor,

00:01:15.923 --> 00:01:19.915
continues to aggressively oppose the recognition of the Holodomor,

00:01:19.915 --> 00:01:25.000
using increasingly aggressive methods of propaganda, including outright lies.

00:01:27.036 --> 00:01:30.914
Lie #1. There was no Holodomor.

00:01:31.861 --> 00:01:33.819
Dozens of villages died of the famine.

00:01:33.819 --> 00:01:40.089
And those who survived were forced to keep silent 
so as not to incite the members of the NKVD

00:01:40.089 --> 00:01:42.208
to pursue their families and friends.

00:01:42.208 --> 00:01:46.602
The Soviet government tried all means to limit the leakage of information

00:01:46.602 --> 00:01:51.561
and falsified statistics on the number of people killed 
by the artificial famine.

00:01:51.561 --> 00:01:54.477
Foreigners also contributed to this.

00:01:54.477 --> 00:02:00.199
For example, the journalist Duranty described the famine
 only as temporary difficulties

00:02:00.199 --> 00:02:01.750
that simply had to be endured.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:04.840
He claimed that there were no deaths in the USSR.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.789
Most foreign diplomats who came to the Soviet Union

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:12.433
did not have access to the real picture or preferred not to notice it.

00:02:12.433 --> 00:02:16.102
They were allowed to see only specially created Potemkin villages,

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:22.493
in which, as in theatrical performances, 
extras were dressed as villagers, and tables were set.

00:02:22.493 --> 00:02:27.573
The topic of the Holodomor was silenced in the Soviet Union until the late 1980s.

00:02:27.573 --> 00:02:30.964
However, archival records have been preserved.

00:02:30.964 --> 00:02:36.191
Among those documents, there were decrees 
and resolutions on food confiscations,

00:02:36.191 --> 00:02:38.955
restrictions on movement for Ukrainian villagers,

00:02:38.955 --> 00:02:42.720
and a ban on foreign journalists from leaving cities.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.908
Together with the memories of thousands of survivors, 
they serve as proof of the crime

00:02:46.908 --> 00:02:54.046
committed in 1932–1933 by the Soviet government 
with Joseph Stalin at its top.

00:03:26.227 --> 00:03:29.312
Lie #2. Poor crops caused the famine.

00:03:29.312 --> 00:03:36.213
This lie has long been supported by Soviet historians, who had no idea of ​​the real events of that period.

00:03:36.213 --> 00:03:44.400
In fact, the weather conditions in 1932–1933 were favorable, 
and the yield was sufficient.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:50.183
The grain harvest in 1932 was actually  less because fewer seeds had been sown,

00:03:50.183 --> 00:03:54.574
so the reason was not the amount of precipitation or atmospheric pressure,

00:03:54.574 --> 00:03:58.248
but the ill-considered agricultural policy of the state.

00:03:58.248 --> 00:04:01.315
People were dying of famine in the villages of Podillia.

00:04:01.315 --> 00:04:07.665
And only 200 meters from there, over the Zbruch River in Poland, 
people had enough food.

00:04:07.665 --> 00:04:15.316
In addition, in 1932–1933, the USSR rejected 
any offers of help from other countries,

00:04:15.316 --> 00:04:18.583
and even more, it actively exported grain.

00:04:18.583 --> 00:04:22.880
Lie #3. The famine spread throughout the whole USSR.

00:04:23.712 --> 00:04:26.970
Many eyewitnesses recall that people in Ukrainian villages suffered

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:32.937
because there was nothing to eat while in neighbouring
Russia and Belarus people had no food problems.

00:04:32.937 --> 00:04:40.437
Interestingly that only in the territory of Ukraine and Russian Kuban, 
inhabited mainly by Ukrainians,

00:04:40.437 --> 00:04:44.488
there was a system of “black boards”, or “boards of infamy”.

00:04:44.488 --> 00:04:50.672
It was forbidden to enter and leave villages, 
and accordingly, to supply any food.

00:04:50.672 --> 00:04:59.102
On 22 January 1933, the Soviet government issued 
a resolution banning people from leaving Ukraine and Kuban.

00:04:59.102 --> 00:05:05.376
In addition, villagers were deprived of the right to buy train tickets 
and barred from entering cities.

00:05:05.376 --> 00:05:09.263
It was the territory where the most Ukrainians lived,

00:05:09.263 --> 00:05:12.680
and where the mortality rate from the famine was the highest.

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:19.778
 This fact proves that the Holodomor was indeed 
the policy of the Soviet government against Ukrainians.

00:05:21.011 --> 00:05:23.754
Lie #4. Ukrainians did not resist.

00:05:24.813 --> 00:05:29.535
In fact, the resistance to collectivisation on the part of Ukrainian villages

00:05:29.535 --> 00:05:34.487
was one of the main reasons why they were exterminated by making people starve.

00:05:34.487 --> 00:05:40.546
In 1930, one third of all village demonstrations against the Soviet rule

00:05:40.546 --> 00:05:43.815
among the republics of the USSR happened in Ukraine.

00:05:43.815 --> 00:05:47.206
More than a million people took part in them.

00:05:47.206 --> 00:05:53.645
In the same year, activists, grain procurement commissioners, and workers of the State Political Administration

00:05:53.645 --> 00:05:59.211
were attacked 2,779 times in Ukrainian villages.

00:05:59.211 --> 00:06:03.571
It was one fifth of all such cases across the USSR.

00:06:03.571 --> 00:06:09.334
For example, the territory of the Dnipropetrovsk region 
in just four months

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:15.620
from October 1932 to January 1933 recorded 
7 murders of activists,

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:21.800
10 attempted murders, 5 injuries, 
6 cases of beatings of government officials.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:25.690
Villagers would set fire to state institutions 
and collective farm buildings.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:31.763
They would come to a collective farm building, protest, 
and take their cattle and grain back.

00:06:31.763 --> 00:06:35.779
Or they would simply refuse to work for nothing 
and sabotage the process.

00:06:35.779 --> 00:06:42.982
In the conditions of constant searches, in order to survive,
 people tried to hide at least some food,

00:06:42.982 --> 00:06:47.669
using pits, basements, attics, or burying supplies.

00:06:47.669 --> 00:06:52.717
Similarly, in the fall, thousands of people 
tried to run away from villages.

00:06:52.717 --> 00:06:57.757
However, all these actions did not grow into a mass
 consolidated movement.

00:06:57.757 --> 00:07:02.280
The remnants of the village resistance were broken 
by total physical destruction.

00:09:34.227 --> 00:09:37.496
Lie #5. The Holodomor was organised by locals.

00:09:38.209 --> 00:09:46.129
Such a myth was advantageous to the Kremlin 
to absolve itself of responsibility for the Holodomor of 1932–1933.

00:09:46.129 --> 00:09:50.860
It was beneficial for them to say that Ukrainians killed their own people.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:54.692
In fact, the ruling elite was multinational.

00:09:54.692 --> 00:09:59.718
They acted primarily as representatives 
of the communist totalitarian regime,

00:09:59.718 --> 00:10:04.049
not some ethnic group or nationality, 
who carried out orders given from above,

00:10:04.049 --> 00:10:05.979
and were part of a single system.

00:10:05.979 --> 00:10:10.978
Even so, some officials tried to mitigate the situation in Ukraine,

00:10:10.978 --> 00:10:15.064
warning that it was critical and asking 
to cut the grain procurement plans.

00:10:15.064 --> 00:10:20.626
Instead, the central government 
in Moscow refused and tightened its grip,

00:10:20.626 --> 00:10:26.640
as evidenced by the archival documents from 
the Communist Party conferences and congresses.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:30.765
Lie #6. There was no mass mortality due to the famine.

00:10:30.765 --> 00:10:36.874
In 1926, almost 31.2 million Ukrainians lived in the USSR,

00:10:36.874 --> 00:10:41.283
and in 1937, there were only 26.4 million left.

00:10:41.283 --> 00:10:49.247
To compare, the number of Russians during this time
 increased from 77.8 million to almost 94 million people,

00:10:49.247 --> 00:10:55.225
Belarusians — from 4.74 million to 4.87 million people.

00:10:55.225 --> 00:11:02.963
In addition, mass graves have been recorded, as evidenced 
by thousands of Holodomor eyewitnesses who managed to survive.

00:11:02.963 --> 00:11:08.537
These facts prove that entire families and streets died out,

00:11:08.537 --> 00:11:11.640
so there should be no doubt that the Holodomor was massive.

00:11:13.055 --> 00:11:17.195
Lie #7. We have known everything about the Holodomor for a long time.

00:11:18.365 --> 00:11:23.510
Some of the valuable oral testimonies of the Holodomor eyewitnesses have already been lost.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:26.858
Millions of people who survived those events died.

00:11:26.858 --> 00:11:35.148
And most of the documents have not yet been processed,
 although the archives of KGB in Ukraine are available to all.

00:11:35.148 --> 00:11:41.168
However, the main and most important ones 
are still kept secret in Moscow.

00:11:41.168 --> 00:11:47.033
Until Russia, the successor to the Soviet Union, 
recognises the Holodomor,

00:11:47.033 --> 00:11:50.440
this piece of information will remain closed to the world.

00:12:42.583 --> 00:12:47.130
Lie #8. The Holodomor was not genocide.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:55.123
Genocide is an intentional act aimed at physically destroying
 an ethnic, national, racial, or religious group.

00:12:55.123 --> 00:13:02.091
The policy pursued by the Soviet Union in the territory of Ukraine 
was directed precisely against Ukrainians.

00:13:02.091 --> 00:13:06.011
No other national group has suffered such losses.

00:13:06.011 --> 00:13:12.263
Nowhere, except in the areas where Ukrainians lived compactly, 
were such methods used.

00:13:12.263 --> 00:13:15.577
The decisions of the top leadership of the USSR,

00:13:15.577 --> 00:13:20.650
medical registers, death registers, eyewitnesses’ accounts,

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:23.726
and hundreds of other documents are proving it.

00:13:23.726 --> 00:13:27.977
Thus, the Holodomor is genocide of the Ukrainian nation,

00:13:27.977 --> 00:13:33.215
and it has been recognised by 17 countries, 
including Ukraine.

